WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.667 --> 00:00:04.834
♪♪

00:00:04.834 --> 00:00:07.100
Narrator: THE FIRST
JIGSAW PUZZLE WAS INVENTED

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:09.400
IN EUROPE IN 1760.

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:11.067
NEARLY TWO CENTURIES LATER,

00:00:11.067 --> 00:00:14.534
A CANADIAN INVENTOR RESHAPED
THE POPULAR PASTIME.

00:00:14.534 --> 00:00:18.734
HIS PUZZLE PIECES, MADE OF THICK
FOAM RATHER THAN CARDBOARD,

00:00:18.734 --> 00:00:21.434
COULD STAND UPRIGHT,
TURNING THE PUZZLE

00:00:21.434 --> 00:00:23.501
INTO A THREE-DIMENSION MODEL.

00:00:23.501 --> 00:00:24.801
♪♪

00:00:24.801 --> 00:00:28.968
CONSTRUCTING A 3-D PUZZLE
PRODUCES IMPRESSIVE RESULTS.

00:00:28.968 --> 00:00:33.567
TO DO SO, TWO 800-PIECE PUZZLE
SETS ARE USED TO CREATE

00:00:33.567 --> 00:00:36.300
THIS SPECTACULAR
CASTLE REPLICA.

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:38.167
♪♪

00:00:38.167 --> 00:00:40.767
AN INDUSTRIAL DESIGNER CREATES
THE PUZZLE'S

00:00:40.767 --> 00:00:42.667
THREE-DIMENSIONAL STRUCTURE.

00:00:42.667 --> 00:00:46.367
AN ILLUSTRATOR USES TECHNIQUES,
SUCH AS VISUAL TEXTURES

00:00:46.367 --> 00:00:49.334
AND SHADING, TO TRANSFORM
FLAT GRAPHICS

00:00:49.334 --> 00:00:52.133
INTO A THREE-DIMENSIONAL
RENDERING.

00:00:52.133 --> 00:00:55.968
THE INDUSTRIAL DESIGNER PREPARES
THE PRINTING AND CUTTING LAYOUT,

00:00:55.968 --> 00:00:58.801
FITTING UP TO THREE
PUZZLES PER SHEET.

00:00:58.801 --> 00:01:02.634
THE PUZZLE PIECES ARE MADE
FROM RIGID FOAM.

00:01:02.634 --> 00:01:05.000
THE FOAM IS SPECIFICALLY
ENGINEERED

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:08.200
TO BE CHEMICALLY COMPATIBLE
WITH THE PAPER GRAPHICS

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:10.167
AND PROPRIETARY ADHESIVE.

00:01:10.167 --> 00:01:11.767
♪♪

00:01:11.767 --> 00:01:13.901
A TECHNICIAN FEEDS
ONE SHEET AT A TIME

00:01:13.901 --> 00:01:16.934
INTO A CUSTOM-DESIGNED
LAMINATION MACHINE.

00:01:16.934 --> 00:01:19.234
THE FIRST STATION
SPREADS HOT GLUE

00:01:19.234 --> 00:01:21.000
OVER THE TOP OF THE FOAM SHEET.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:22.634
♪♪

00:01:22.634 --> 00:01:25.467
AN AUTOMATED ARM WITH
VACUUM SUCTION CUPS

00:01:25.467 --> 00:01:27.934
LIFTS A SINGLE SHEET
OF PRINTED PAPER

00:01:27.934 --> 00:01:31.400
AND PLACES IT ON
THE GLUE-COATED FOAM SHEET.

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:34.701
AS SOON AS THE PAPER
ADHERES TO THE FOAM,

00:01:34.701 --> 00:01:38.033
THE SHEET IS RELEASED
FROM THE SUCTION CUPS.

00:01:38.033 --> 00:01:40.834
♪♪

00:01:40.834 --> 00:01:43.200
THEN THE FOAM MOVES
UNDER A ROLLER

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:45.033
THAT PRESSES DOWN THE PAPER.

00:01:45.033 --> 00:01:46.868
♪♪

00:01:46.868 --> 00:01:49.801
AS THE LAMINATED FOAM
EXITS THE MACHINE,

00:01:49.801 --> 00:01:53.100
A TECHNICIAN ROLLS A TUBE
OVER THE FOAM,

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:55.501
PRESSING OUT ANY REMAINING
AIR BUBBLES

00:01:55.501 --> 00:01:58.133
TO ENSURE THE PAPER
ADHERES FULLY.

00:01:58.133 --> 00:02:00.167
♪♪

00:02:00.167 --> 00:02:03.133
IN THE DEVELOPMENT PHASE,
THE INDUSTRIAL DESIGNER

00:02:03.133 --> 00:02:05.968
ASSEMBLED A BLUEPRINT
FOR HOW THE PUZZLE PIECES

00:02:05.968 --> 00:02:09.000
WOULD BE SHAPED AND LAID OUT.

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:11.100
THAT DESIGN WENT TO A TOOLMAKER,

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:13.334
WHO PRODUCED A CORRESPONDING
CUTTING DIE

00:02:13.334 --> 00:02:15.033
OUT OF STEEL KNIVES.

00:02:15.033 --> 00:02:18.133
♪♪

00:02:18.133 --> 00:02:21.133
THE DIE IS MOUNTED
INSIDE THE CUTTING MACHINE.

00:02:21.133 --> 00:02:22.868
♪♪

00:02:22.868 --> 00:02:24.767
A TECHNICIAN FEEDS THE MACHINE

00:02:24.767 --> 00:02:27.200
ONE LAMINATED FOAM SHEET
AT A TIME,

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:29.100
PAPER SIDE DOWN.

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:30.601
♪♪

00:02:30.601 --> 00:02:32.834
GRIPPERS GRAB
THE EDGE OF THE PAPER,

00:02:32.834 --> 00:02:35.267
PULLING THE SHEET INTO
THE MACHINE.

00:02:35.267 --> 00:02:39.133
THE CUTTING DIE SLICES THE
PUZZLE PIECES INTO THE FOAM.

00:02:39.133 --> 00:02:40.567
♪♪

00:02:40.567 --> 00:02:43.601
EVEN THOUGH THE CUTTING
PRESSURE COMPRESSES THE FOAM,

00:02:43.601 --> 00:02:47.801
IT IMMEDIATELY BOUNCES BACK,
KEEPING THE SHEET INTACT.

00:02:47.801 --> 00:02:49.400
♪♪

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:51.701
THANKS TO A HIGH-QUALITY
RUBBER SHEET

00:02:51.701 --> 00:02:53.767
INSERTED BETWEEN THE BLADES,

00:02:53.767 --> 00:02:57.200
THE PIECES DON'T GET STUCK
IN THE DIE.

00:02:57.200 --> 00:02:59.834
THE STIFF RUBBER
PROVIDES COUNTER-PRESSURE

00:02:59.834 --> 00:03:02.100
TO HELP REMOVE THE FOAM SHEET.

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:04.767
♪♪

00:03:04.767 --> 00:03:07.834
IF THE SHEET HAS TWO OR THREE
PUZZLES PRINTED ON IT,

00:03:07.834 --> 00:03:10.901
THE CUTTING DIE SEPARATES THEM.

00:03:10.901 --> 00:03:13.634
THEN A TECHNICIAN PLACES
THE PUZZLE

00:03:13.634 --> 00:03:15.901
ON A SEMI-AUTOMATIC
CONVEYOR BELT

00:03:15.901 --> 00:03:18.634
THAT MOVES IT TO
THE DISMANTLING MACHINE.

00:03:18.634 --> 00:03:23.000
THE MACHINE INFUSES THE DIE-CUT
PUZZLE SHEET WITH STEAM.

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:25.300
THE STEAM PREVENTS
STATIC ELECTRICITY,

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:28.367
WHICH CAUSES
PIECES TO CLING TOGETHER

00:03:28.367 --> 00:03:30.734
OR TO THE INSIDE OF THE MACHINE.

00:03:30.734 --> 00:03:33.734
THE MACHINE SEPARATES THE PIECES

00:03:33.734 --> 00:03:38.067
AND DISPENSES THEM INTO
A PUZZLE BOX.

00:03:38.067 --> 00:03:41.200
A TECHNICIAN ADDS THE STANDARD
INSTRUCTION SHEET

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:43.033
AND SEALS THE BOX.

00:03:43.033 --> 00:03:46.000
♪♪

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:48.234
THE INSTRUCTIONS ARE
IN BLACK AND WHITE

00:03:48.234 --> 00:03:51.567
BUT CAN BE VIEWED
IN COLOR ONLINE.

00:03:51.567 --> 00:03:55.601
THE FIRST STEP IS TO SORT
THE PIECES BY COLOR AND DESIGN

00:03:55.601 --> 00:03:58.300
AND SET ASIDE THE ONES
MARKED WITH A RED DOT

00:03:58.300 --> 00:04:00.934
WHICH IS PART OF
THE MANUFACTURING PROCESS,

00:04:00.934 --> 00:04:03.667
NOT THE PUZZLE ITSELF.

00:04:03.667 --> 00:04:08.300
THE NEXT STEP IS TO ASSEMBLE
THE PUZZLE, SECTION BY SECTION.

00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:09.968
ALL THE SECTIONS ARE FLAT,

00:04:09.968 --> 00:04:13.534
SO THE FINAL STEP IS TO
ATTACH THE FLAT SECTIONS

00:04:13.534 --> 00:04:16.534
TO MAKE THE PUZZLE
THREE-DIMENSIONAL.

00:04:16.534 --> 00:04:18.767
FOR AN ADDITIONAL CHALLENGE,

00:04:18.767 --> 00:04:21.901
YOU CAN FORGO
THE STEP-BY-STEP INSTRUCTIONS

00:04:21.901 --> 00:04:24.701
AND REFER ONLY TO
THE PHOTOS ON THE BOX.

00:04:24.701 --> 00:04:25.701
♪♪

00:04:25.701 --> 00:04:28.167
IF YOU HAPPEN TO
LOSE A PUZZLE PIECE,

00:04:28.167 --> 00:04:30.300
YOU CAN GO TO
THE COMPANY'S WEBSITE

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:32.834
TO TRACE THE NUMBER
OF YOUR MISSING PIECE,

00:04:32.834 --> 00:04:35.634
THEN ORDER A NEW PIECE ONLINE.

00:04:35.634 --> 00:04:37.133
THE COMPANY WILL MAIL IT TO YOU

00:04:37.133 --> 00:04:39.467
SO THAT YOU CAN
COMPLETE YOUR PUZZLE.

00:04:39.467 --> 00:04:40.567
♪♪

00:04:40.567 --> 00:04:42.934
UNLIKE A TRADITIONAL
FLAT PUZZLE,

00:04:42.934 --> 00:04:46.634
YOU CAN MOVE YOUR 3-D PUZZLE
WITHOUT IT FALLING APART.

00:04:46.634 --> 00:04:48.701
♪♪

00:04:48.701 --> 00:04:50.968
IT TAKES FOUR TO SIX MONTHS

00:04:50.968 --> 00:04:54.968
TO DEVELOPMENT AND DESIGN
THIS INCREDIBLE 3-D PUZZLE.

00:04:54.968 --> 00:04:57.400
NOW IT'S TIME TO SPEND
EVEN LONGER

00:04:57.400 --> 00:05:00.267
PIECING THIS PUZZLE TOGETHER.

00:05:00.267 --> 00:05:01.801
♪♪

